# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` -- the Windows default -- converts text
# files to CRLF on checkout. Prettier is configured `endOfLine: "lf"`, so the
# very first `npm run verify` after a clone fails on hundreds of files that
# nobody edited. That is a miserable first experience and it teaches people to
# distrust the checks, which is worse than the whitespace.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf, so behaviour no longer depends on each
# developer's git configuration. Verified by cloning this repository on Windows
# with autocrlf=true and running `npm run format:check`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
